### Reward Design

**Formula**: `gated_ssim × phash_similarity × duration_penalty`

| Component | Metric | Gate / Scaling |
|-----------|--------|----------------|
| gated_ssim | RGB SSIM over 60 sampled frames with temporal offset search (±5 frames) | Gate at 0.70; cubic ramp `((ssim - 0.70) / 0.30)^3` above gate |
| phash_similarity | Per-frame perceptual hash (8×8 DCT), mean Hamming distance → similarity | None (linear: `1 - mean_dist/32`) |
| duration_penalty | Frame count ratio between agent and reference videos | Hard fail outside [0.75×, 1.25×]; linear ramp within band |

**Design rationale**: The 0.70 SSIM gate prevents trivially similar outputs (e.g., same background color) from scoring. Cubic exponent rewards high-fidelity reproduction — marginal gains above 0.90 are worth far more than gains around 0.75. Multiplicative composition means all three factors must be high: a perfect visual match with wrong duration scores 0, and vice versa. Six anti-cheat static analysis gates (source size ≤50KB, numeric literals ≤580, flat array ≤150, max string ≤335, total strings ≤1220, non-nice floats ≤30) enforce algorithmic solutions over data extraction.

<!-- BEGIN:ANTI_CHEAT -->
### Isolation Checklist

| Check | Status | Detail |
|-------|--------|--------|
| agent.user in task.toml | PASS | `user = "agent"` set under `[agent]` |
| Dockerfile user setup | PASS | `useradd agent`, `chown -R agent:agent /app`, `chmod 700 /tests`, `chown agent:agent /solution` — all present |
| Dockerfile strace | PASS | `strace` installed via apt; needed because verifier runs `npm run render` (agent code) |
| test.sh /logs lockdown | PASS | `chmod 700 "$VERIFIER_DIR"` then `rm -rf "$VERIFIER_DIR"/*` as first two actions |
| test.sh strace wrapping | PASS | `strace -f -e trace=openat` wraps render with `timeout 600`; `compute_reward.py` runs as a separate step outside strace |
| Scoring imports /app | PASS | `compute_reward.py` reads `/tests/reference.mp4` and `/run/verified_project.tsx` (snapshot); agent video copied to `/tests/agent_output.mp4` before scoring — no imports from `/app` |

### Anti-Cheat Measures

**Source integrity (test.sh)**
- Regex grep blocks banned patterns in `project.tsx`: filesystem APIs (`fs.*`, `readFileSync`), process spawning (`child_process`, `exec`, `spawn`, `fork`), eval/Function, video decoding libraries (`ffmpeg`, `sharp`, `jimp`), and encoding primitives (`base64`, `Buffer.from`, `atob`, `btoa`) — prevents reference extraction and runtime escape
- Source snapshot to `/run/verified_project.tsx` before any workspace mutation — scoring always evaluates the code the agent actually wrote, not a post-tamper version

**Clean-room execution environment (test.sh)**
- Wipes `/app` (except node_modules), `/home/agent`, `/solution`, `/tmp`, `/dev/shm`, `/var/tmp` and restores workspace from `/tests/pristine_app.tar` — eliminates planted files, modified configs, and injected modules
- Restores `node_modules` from `/tests/node_modules_backup` if missing — prevents poisoned package substitution surviving into render
- `pkill -9 -u agent` before render — kills agent background processes that could race to manipulate output or reward files
- Symlink check on `/app/output/video.mp4` — prevents agent pointing output at reference video

**Runtime process auditing (test.sh)**
- `strace -f -e trace=openat` wraps render; post-render analysis greps for `openat(.*reward\.(txt|json).*O_WRONLY` — detects any attempt by agent code to write reward files during rendering
- `timeout 600` inside strace — prevents DoS via infinite loops or sleeps in forked children

**Data-dump detection (compute_reward.py)**
- `source_size_gate`: rejects source > 50KB — caps total code volume
- `dump_literal_gate`: rejects > 580 numeric literals — catches per-frame coordinate dumps
- `flat_array_gate`: rejects any single bracketed numeric array > 150 elements — catches encoded frame data in arrays
- `string_lit_gate`: rejects any string literal > 335 chars — catches base64 or encoded data in strings
- `total_str_gate`: rejects total string literal content > 1220 chars — catches distributed data encoding across many strings
- `non_nice_float_gate`: rejects > 30 floats that aren't multiples of 0.25 (excluding 0.0 and ~0.01) — catches extracted positional data that produces non-round values

**Scoring design**
- Multiplicative formula `score = gated_ssim × phash_sim × duration_penalty` — all three factors must independently be high; a zero in any factor zeros the total, preventing partial-credit gaming
- SSIM gated at 0.70 with cubic scaling: `((mean - 0.70) / 0.30)^3` — near-miss outputs score near zero (e.g., 0.80 SSIM → 0.037 gated), requiring genuinely close visual match
- Duration penalty hard-fails outside [0.75x, 1.25x] frame count ratio — prevents trivially short or extended videos from scoring; linear ramp within bounds penalizes imprecise timing
- Temporal offset search (±5 frames) picks best alignment — tolerates minor timing drift without requiring frame-perfect sync
- pHash similarity via DCT-based perceptual hashing catches structural differences that pixel SSIM might miss

**Undefended attack surfaces**
- `allow_internet = true` in task.toml — agent can download pre-built solutions, reference analysis tools, or model outputs from external servers at runtime; source anti-cheat gates only scan `project.tsx`, so a fetched clean algorithmic solution is undetectable
- Poisoned `node_modules` survives clean-room wipe — the `find` delete excludes `node_modules` and the backup restore only triggers if the directory is entirely missing; agent can modify Revideo renderer internals to produce a matching video regardless of `project.tsx` content
- Strace grep matches `O_WRONLY` but not `O_RDWR` — `openat()` with `O_RDWR` flag also permits writing to reward files and would bypass the strace audit check

**Verdict: WARN**
<!-- END:ANTI_CHEAT -->

### Verifier & Scoring Integrity

| Check | Status | Detail |
|-------|--------|--------|
| Correctness gating | PASS | All three components are multiplicative; SSIM hard-gated at 0.70 (below → 0.0). Duration hard-fails outside [0.75×, 1.25×]. Any single zero → final score 0. |
| Test quality | PASS | 60-frame SSIM sampling + perceptual hashing + duration ratio. Six static anti-cheat gates on source code. Comprehensive for visual similarity task. |
| Determinism | PASS | No randomness in scoring. SSIM/pHash are deterministic on same frames. No timing-sensitive tests. Temporal offset search uses fixed set [-5,-3,-1,0,1,3,5]. |
| Isolation hardening | PASS | See Isolation Checklist in Anti-Cheat section |
| Reward hacking surface | WARN | Undefended attack surfaces noted (see Anti-Cheat section). |
| Baseline reward | PASS | Unmodified stub renders ~24 frames of black; reference has ~480 frames. Duration ratio 0.05 < 0.75 → duration_penalty=0.0 → final score=0.0. |

### Workspace

| Check | Status | Detail |
|-------|--------|--------|
| Build readiness | PASS | `npm ci` runs at build time with package-lock.json (4177 lines). Chromium pre-installed. Stub `project.tsx` compiles and renders. `npm run render` = `tsc && node dist/render.js`. |
| Instruction ↔ workspace | PASS | Instruction lists: @revideo/core, @revideo/2d, @revideo/renderer, Chromium, ffmpeg, ffprobe — all installed in Dockerfile and package.json. `src/render.ts` present and configured. |
| Reference docs | PASS | 69 reference documentation files covering Revideo API (components, signals, flow, tweening, positioning, etc.) in `reference-documentation/`. qa.toml confirms coverage of all APIs used in oracle solution. |

### Notes

- **`allow_internet = true`**: Waivered in qa.toml. Revideo renders via Puppeteer controlling headless Chromium over localhost. Harbor's `allow_internet=false` applies `network_mode:none` which kills loopback — Puppeteer cannot connect to Chromium and rendering fails. The agent does not need external internet; only localhost is used.
- **`source_scene.tsx` and `solution_project.tsx` in `environment/`**: These are consumed only at Docker build time (to generate `reference.mp4` and bake the oracle solution into the image). They are not copied into `/app` — the Dockerfile explicitly deletes them after use. The agent never sees them at runtime.
- **Solution identity**: `source_scene.tsx`, `solution_project.tsx`, and `solution/project.tsx` are all byte-identical, ensuring the oracle produces a reference video that exactly matches what it later submits as a solution.

